# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# backend/data/raw/*.csv is deliberately NOT ignored.
#
# data.AS_OF pins the project to one dataset so the report, the slides, the
# figures and the dashboard all describe the same numbers. Yahoo re-adjusts the
# whole price history for dividends and splits, so a clone that re-downloaded
# would get a rewritten past and disagree with every number written down — the
# exact failure the pin exists to prevent. ~2.4 MB of public market data,
# committed on purpose. Set AS_OF = None to track live data again.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/

# Node
node_modules/
dist/
dist-ssr/
*.tsbuildinfo
*.local

# Generated intermediate. REPORT.pdf and SLIDES.pdf are committed as the
# deliverables; REPORT.html is only the step in between, and it is 1.3 MB of
# base64 that regenerates in a second.
docs/REPORT.html

# Logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# Tooling residue
.remember/
.playwright-mcp/
.impeccable/
.claude/

# Editor and OS
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.sw?
